  "id": "e:forsøge sig frem|phrase#1",
  "kind": "example",
  "unit": "entry:forsøge sig frem|phrase",
  "passed": false,
  "stage": "review",
  "problems": [
   "sense: Danish 'forsøge mig frem' means 'try my way forward by trial and error', but the sentence context 'I don't know the recipe, so I have to try it out' does not clearly convey the 'trial and error' meaning",
   "translations: English translation 'try it out' does not capture the 'trial and error' meaning of 'forsøge sig frem'",
   "translations: Russian translation 'обязательно попробую' means 'I will definitely try', which does not match the Danish 'må forsøge mig frem' (have to try my way forward) in meaning or modality",
   "translations: Ukrainian translation 'мушу спробувати' means 'must try', which does not capture the 'trial and error' meaning of 'forsøge mig frem'",
   "The English translation 'try it out' drops the 'forward'/'by trial and error' nuance of 'forsøge sig frem'.",
   "The Russian translation 'обязательно попробую' means 'I will definitely try', which changes the meaning from 'have to try my way forward' to a statement of intent."
  ]
 },
